      "tactic_notes": "<div align=\"left\">\n<h2>1. Focus on applying Burns early on in the fight</h2>\n<p><strong>Pepel Zorya&nbsp;</strong>get stronger as everyone get more <strong>Burn&nbsp;</strong>duration. Use these moves during earlier rounds to apply&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong> on everyone (including itself):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Heat Wave:&nbsp;</strong>Low damage, but apply <strong>Burn&nbsp;</strong>to everyone on hit. Best to use when only one or few creature is&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong>ing.</li>\n<li><strong>Searing Missile:&nbsp;</strong>Medium damage, very versatile attack that can be used on both players and boss. Consume lots of MP.</li>\n<li><strong>Piercing Fire:&nbsp;</strong>High damage. Force enemy to share the damage and&nbsp;<strong>Burn.</strong> Cannot target friendly unit.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Summon Fire Emblems as soon as possible</h2>\n<p><strong>Pepel Zorya&nbsp;</strong>can be very weak without her <strong>Fire Emblems</strong>. Once the amount of&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong> is enough, summon&nbsp;<strong>Fire Emblem&nbsp;</strong>right away!</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fire Emblem: Baptism of Fire:&nbsp;</strong>Usable when<strong> Pepel Zorya</strong> has 5 stacks of <strong>Burn</strong>. Force the player to deal enough damage each turn.</li>\n<li><strong>Fire Emblem: Lingering Flame: </strong>Usable when <strong>everyone </strong>in the conflict has at least 1 stack of <strong>Burn</strong>. Force player to attack many time to break the defensive barrier.</li>\n<li><strong>Fire Emblem: Divine Condemn:&nbsp;</strong>Usable when <strong>any enemy</strong> has 5 stacks of&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong>. Anti-Tank mechanic that proc <strong>Burn&nbsp;</strong>on enemy when taking any&nbsp;<strong>Fire&nbsp;</strong>attacks.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Mix up once Fire Emblems are set!</h2>\n<p>Use <strong>Veil of Smoke</strong> and <strong>Dousing Oil</strong> to mix up the fight after 1 or 2 Fire Emblems are summoned.<strong> Dousing Oil</strong> is exceptionally good on player with <strong>Fire </strong>resistance</p>\n<h2>4. Keep your <strong>Lingering Flame</strong> up!</h2>\n<p><strong>Lingering Flame</strong> helps mitigate damage for <strong>Pepel Zorya</strong> but it must be topped up with <strong>Friendly Fire&nbsp;</strong>from attacks including: <strong>Heat Wave, Searing Missile&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>Veil of Smoke</strong>.</p>\n<h2>5. Once all 3 Fire Emblems are ready, use <strong>Zero Power</strong>!</h2>\n<p><strong>【💥Zero Power】 Merciless Sun</strong> deals unavoidable, resistance pieacing damage on all player. <strong>However</strong>, <strong>Pepel Zorya</strong> will enter <strong>Break </strong>afterward<strong>&nbsp;</strong>to let the player breath (or go all out).</p>\n<h2>6. Some tools that player can use to counter <strong>Pepel Zorya</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Any skill that can remove&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong> consistently will make the fight managable.&nbsp;<strong>Reefesia&nbsp;</strong>will get a seed that allow her to remove&nbsp;<strong>Burn</strong> on multiple target later.</li>\n<li><strong>Ice&nbsp;</strong>damage can easily remove <strong>Pepel Zorya&nbsp;</strong>Hit Points faster than she can regain.&nbsp;<strong>Lingering Flame&nbsp;</strong>can help prevent this.</li>\n<li><strong>Fire</strong> resistance/immune will make that specific character nigh invincible. Spam <strong>Dousing Oil</strong> to prevent that.</li>\n<li><strong>Commander Heroic Skill: Iron Forest&nbsp;</strong><strong>can outright prevent Pepel Zorya from casting spell forever</strong> or until they run out of Mind Points to use.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
